␛[0;1;34mHTML images␛[0m

  An ␛[0;35;48;5;236m⍽<img>⍽␛[0m tag on a line of its own is shown
  like a Markdown image:

  ␛[0;2;3m[image: Icon]␛[0m

  So is an image wrapped the way READMEs
  centre a logo; kiri does not centre it:

  ␛[0;2;3m[image: Test pattern]␛[0m

  A ␛[0;35;48;5;236m⍽<picture>⍽␛[0m shows its ␛[0;35;48;5;236m⍽<img>⍽␛[0m, whatever
